{"name":"Nomad Grey","hex":"#7e736f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"nomad","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A member of a society or class who herd animals from pasture to pasture with no fixed home.","Synonym of wanderer: an itinerant person."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Synonym of nomadic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nomad"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nomad","blocks":[{"text":"Nomads are communities without fixed habitation who regularly move to and from areas. Such groups include hunter-gatherers, pastoral nomads, tinkers and trader nomads. In the twentieth century, the population of nomadic pastoral tribes slowly decreased, reaching an estimated 30–40 million nomads in the world as of 1995."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Encampment_of_Gypsies_with_Caravans.jpg/330px-Encampment_of_Gypsies_with_Caravans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nomad","wikidata":"Q128393"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Hungarian_Gypsy_Mother_and_Child_N